  "rationale": "The batch shows a structural overgeneralization in <END>: its very heavy rule for any prefix ending in punctuation also matches commas, making it dominate at introductory commas where a character name follows. Reduce that rule and add moderate support for the observed general pattern of a name after a comma; this should help across character names without asserting which particular name must follow. To preserve endings, add a separate rule for several observed closing constructions before final punctuation (including “story ends.”, “the end.”, “all for now.”, and “time!”). These cues are not proof that every occurrence is final, so the added mass is limited. Other comma contexts and unseen ending forms remain potential counterexamples; replay behavior should be checked by the gate.",
